{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01 - implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n- For each call: subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call to get gain\n- Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least one token)\n- Accept a call if: parseable=true AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n- Return accepted_call_ids and diagnostics in original call order\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\n1. For each call:\n   - gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n   - normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n   - accepted = parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n\n2. diagnostics: list of {call_id, normalized_gain, accepted} in original order\n3. accepted_call_ids: list of call_ids where accepted=True\n\nLet me verify with the fixture data:\n\nCase 000, threshold=0.05:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, tokens=5, norm=0.3125319, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, tokens=4, norm=0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, tokens=6, norm=0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, tokens=5, norm=0.1519079 (approx 0.15190786), parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, tokens=5, norm=0.04196760, parseable=true → NOT accepted (0.0419... \u003c 0.05)\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, tokens=4, norm=0.190983035, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call5\"]\n\nNow the schema says normalized_gain should be rounded. The candidate says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" But what rounding? The output schema says type \"number\" so it could be any float. Let me not round and just return the float value.\n\nActually looking at the schema again - it says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" in the candidate artifact. But the schema just says `\"type\": \"number\"`. I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, maybe 8 or just leave as-is.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        norm_tokens = max(tokens, 1)\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions properties like \"normalized_weights\", \"stronger_counterfactual\", \"inclusive_threshold\", \"stable_order\":\n- normalized_weights: dividing by prediction_tokens\n- stronger_counterfactual: gain = loss_without - loss_with (positive means the call helps)\n- inclusive_threshold: \u003e= threshold (not \u003e)\n- stable_order: keep original call order in diagnostics\n\nThe description says \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" which means `max(prediction_tokens, 1)` to avoid division by zero.\n\nI think this is correct. Let me write the final JSON response.\n\nThe response needs to be a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        norm_tokens = max(tokens, 1)\\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01ABEt4jHDjw1FDxRywSrNYt","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2352},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2352,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":37,"output_tokens":1337,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1069},"service_tier":"standard"}}